{"name":"Lights at Sea","hex":"#01968b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of light"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The lungs, now chiefly of an animal (being lighter than adjacent parts)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lights"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lights (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Lights Valerie Anne Poxleitner-Bokan known professionally as Lights is a Canadian singer and songwriter. Her debut album, The Listening (2009), reached the top 10 on the Billboard Canadian Albums chart and was certified platinum by the Canadian Recording Industry Association (CRIA) for selling over 80,000 copies as of 2017. The album included the singles \"Drive My Soul\" and \"February Air\" which were featured in a series of Old Navy television ads. Her second album, Siberia, which featured the single \"Toes\", was released in 2011. A more dubstep influenced record, Siberia has received generally positive reviews from music critics and achieved moderate success, entering the top 50 on the Billboard 200 and selling more than 10,000 units in its first week."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Lights_%40_The_Roxy_05_20_2025_%2854846490282%29.jpg/330px-Lights_%40_The_Roxy_05_20_2025_%2854846490282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(musician)","wikidata":"Q242437"},{"title":"At Sea","blocks":[{"text":"At Sea is a 2007 American experimental documentary film directed by Peter Hutton. Shot on 16 mm film over the course of three years, it follows the \"birth, life and death\" of a container ship, from its construction in a South Korean dockyard to its travels on the Atlantic Ocean and eventual beaching in Bangladesh, where ship breakers labor for scrap."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/At_Sea","wikidata":"Q137803725"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/LIGHTS_II.jpg/500px-LIGHTS_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/LIGHTS_II.jpg/500px-LIGHTS_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Lights performing in Toronto at Sonic Boom Records, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALIGHTS_II.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg/500px-LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg/1280px-LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg/500px-LIGHTS_IMG_6799_%2815999651243%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u